{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Flow step debugger core with FRAMES (P2; spec: dev/_ASSETS/docs/flow-language.md 1.5.4). step(state, pick) -> {status, state, event, ready, default, ended, depth}: advances a flow ONE step over a frame stack and emits one event (enter, seed, deliver, sync, iter, eval, leave, next, terminate, fail, finish, done, stall, error). Start with state = {body: the flow's root Case JSON, args}, then pass back the returned state {body, frames, seq}; graphs are never mutated, the stepper's bookkeeping is copied per step and value handles are shared (flowlang aliasing). Local ops with localdata and command ops whose callee is a flow (any library; raw args, no auth re-check - the parent call is the gate) open a frame: enter ... leave, then the op's closing eval (a fail inside becomes b=false at the caller's condition; command outputs map by position). List/loop ops run as iterations: iter, then one eval or enter..leave+eval; the last iteration's eval carries done and the collected outputs; finish stops a loop only via a local frame's finish flag. rust/python command ops stay one opaque eval. Only the top frame steps and an op in progress is atomic (ready = [{kind:auto}]). pick = {} takes the DEFAULT pick (flowlang's sweep order, so continuing with {} is the Code::execute run); {kind: wire|sync|op, index} picks a READY item of the top frame - anything else is refused with status err and the state unchanged. No re-run (a second delivery is reported as I-1); I-4 gives an error event, a stuck case a stall event (either ends the run); depth limit 64 frames. Step modes (over/out/run_to) are in drive.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;\nuse std::panic;","params":[{"name":"state","type":"JSONObject"},{"name":"pick","type":"JSONObject"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"kwjhgp1a16a026788s1c8","readers":[],"time":1792870430935,"username":"system","writers":[]}